embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8114, "total_tokens": 8114}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 3471 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Elastic Scaling of Application Servers\nDescription: Via the elastic scaling feature, a system will scale dynamically by adding additional application servers when the system load increases. When the load decreases again, the system scales down. Scaling happens up to a system-specific maximum ACU value. Charges will relate to the actual allocated ABAP compute units.  For more information, see Creating an ABAP System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3472 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Elastic Scaling of Application Servers\nDescription: Via the elastic scaling feature, a system will scale dynamically by adding additional application servers when the system load increases. When the load decreases again, the system scales down. Scaling happens up to a system-specific maximum ACU value. Charges will relate to the actual allocated ABAP compute units.  For more information, see Creating an ABAP System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3473 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Enterprise Event Enablement: Filter for Outbound Bindings\nDescription: You can now filter events before they are published to the event consumer. You can configure event filters for each channel and event topic using the Fiori app Enterprise Event Enablement  Maintain Event Channel Binding.  For more information, see Maintain Filters for Outbound Event Topics.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3474 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Enterprise Event Enablement: Filter for Outbound Bindings\nDescription: You can now filter events before they are published to the event consumer. You can configure event filters for each channel and event topic using the Fiori app Enterprise Event Enablement  Maintain Event Channel Binding.  For more information, see Maintain Filters for Outbound Event Topics.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3475 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Generate SOAP Provider Proxies\nDescription: You can now generate SOAP provider proxies from WSDL files using the so-called SOAP Provider Model.  For more information, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3476 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Generate SOAP Provider Proxies\nDescription: You can now generate SOAP provider proxies from WSDL files using the so-called SOAP Provider Model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3477 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Generator for Custom OData UI Services Based on RAP BO Interfaces\nDescription: You can now generate custom OData UI services based on RAP BO interfaces using a generator wizard in ADT.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-02-16\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3478 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Health Monitoring\nDescription: In SAP Cloud ALM, you can now use an additional metric for e-mail transmissions.   See Central Health Monitoring Using SAP Focused Run and SAP Cloud ALM .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3479 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Health Monitoring\nDescription: In the Health Monitoring app, you can now use additional metrics for e-mail transmissions and changes to database table entries.   See Local Health Monitoring.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3480 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Health Monitoring\nDescription: In SAP Cloud ALM, you can now use an additional metric for e-mail transmissions.   See Central Health Monitoring Using SAP Focused Run and SAP Cloud ALM .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-18\nValid as Of: 2024-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 841 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: RAP Business Objects Test Double Framework: Supported EML Statements\nDescription: The RAP Business Objects test double framework now supports these EML statements: Get Permissions, Key Functions and Set Locks.  See Writing Tests with Mock EML APIs Support.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 842 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Restructuring the \"Code Completion\" and \"Source Code Editors\" Preference Pages\nDescription: Some checkboxes and radio buttons on the Code Completion and Source Code Editors preference pages have been revised and relocated between the two pages. Additionally, the wording of some items and section titles has been revised. These changes enhance the usability and user experience when configuring preferences for code completion.  See:     Keyword Completion      Non-Keyword Completion      Using Automatic Code Completion      Inserting a Full Signature Automatically      Inserting or Overwriting Source Code      Closing Brackets and Literals Automatically    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 843 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Supporting 'Between' Capabilities\nDescription: Data Preview now supports ‘between’ capabilities in the filter options.  See Using the Add Filter Button.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 844 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Testing Web API-Based Services Using Swagger UI\nDescription: You can now test Web API-based services from service binding using Swagger UI.  See Using Service Binding Editor for OData V2 Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 845 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Working with the Log When Migrating CDS DDIC-Based Views to CDS View Entities\nDescription: After finishing the simulation or migration of CDS DDIC-based views to CDS view entities, you can now filter the log on the result page using the Show Objects drop-down list box. These options enhance readability by limiting the number of displayed results.  In addition, you can now rerun a simulation or migration. This helps you to restart the process for a set of CDS DDIC-based views at the beginning. For example, you can trigger the productive migration from the result page of a simulation.  See Migrating CDS DDIC-Based Views to CDS View Entities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 846 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Business Configurations: Intent Navigation\nDescription: If all technical key fields are provided as parameters to uniquely identify a record of an object page or subobject page, it's opened directly.See Custom Business Configurations App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 847 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Custom Code Analysis: 3-Tier Model ATC Checks\nDescription: There are now two new ATC checks of category 3-Tier Model: \"Usage of APIs\" and \"Allowed Enhancement Technologies\".  \"Usage of APIs\" verifies the usage of classic Tier 2 and Tier 3 ABAP development objects based on the usage guidelines of SAP APIs. It analyzes all ABAP development objects, except for those with ABAP language version \"Key User\" or \"ABAP Cloud Development\", by identifying their used APIs. For APIs that should not be used, the ATC check shares information on successors, if any.  \"Allowed Enhancement Technologies\" identifies whether only the BAdI enhancement technology has been used in the code.  Please update your allowed RFC function modules in your cloud connector accordingly. To do this, apply 2861842 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 848 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Data Archiving: Storage Manager Implementation\nDescription: You can now use a new interface method to rollback faulty verified archive files.See Storage Manager Implementation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: ", "2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 848 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Data Archiving: Storage Manager Implementation\nDescription: You can now use a new interface method to rollback faulty verified archive files.See Storage Manager Implementation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 849 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Hide Empty Spaces and Pages in the SAP Fiori Launchpad\nDescription: Spaces and pages are not shown when they are empty because of the user's role context. This feature is now enabled by default. The launchpad setting SPACES_HIDE_EMPTY_SPACES_PAGES is set to the default value true that can be changed in the Manage Launchpad Settings app. With the 2508 release, the setting will be removed from the Manage Launchpad Settings app, and empty spaces and pages will continue to be hidden by default.  For more information, see Empty Spaces and Pages Not Displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-14\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 850 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: IAM Information System\nDescription: You can now display the relevant components for business catalogs and applications. This way you can check under which component you can create an incident if required.For more information, see IAM Information System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n", "--- Record 91 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Destination Service - REST API\nDescription:   Added support for referencing resources from multiple isolation levels via a single call to the Destination service API (for example, having a destination on subaccount level and extending it with a fragment on the instance level). For more information, see Referring Resources Using the REST API.  Added a field in the publicKeys endpoint of the certificate retrieval APIs, containing the subject DN of the leaf certificate.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 92 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Introduction of a new top-level parameter region-domain\nDescription: A new top-level parameter region-domain is introduced. It is resolved to the domain of the current region. (See the Domain column in Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment). When a region has multiple CF API endpoints, the parameter will point to the domain of the respective endpoint used for the deployment. The parameter is different from the existing parameters default-domain and region-primary-domain:      The parameter default-domain usually depends on the current organization setup and the existing shared domains for it. It is not reliable for regions without shared domains, for example regions China (Shanghai) and China (North 3). On the other hand, the region-domain parameter is more sustainable and does not depend on the current organization setup.  The parameters region-primary-domain and region-domain are equal when used in most of the regions. They are different when MTA deployments are done in target org/space in different CF APIs in one region.      Examples:  If the MTA deployment is done in a target org/space with CF API endpoint that is equal to api.eu10.hana.ondemand.com, the value of the domain would be:    default-domain: cfapps.eu10.hana.ondemand.com      region-domain: eu10.hana.ondemand.com      region-primary-domain: eu10.hana.ondemand.com      If the MTA deployment is done in a target org/space with CF API endpoint that is equal to api.eu10-004.hana.ondemand.com, the value of the domain would be:    default-domain: cfapps.eu10-004.hana.ondemand.com      region-domain: eu10-004.hana.ondemand.com      region-primary-domain: eu10.hana.ondemand.com      See Parameters and Properties.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: 2509a\n\n--- Record 93 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Events Page at Application Level: Improvements\nDescription: The updated Events page at the application level in the cockpit provides the following improvements:    Events page renamed to Application Events for improved clarity      Target column added to the page. It shows for which application the event is triggered.      Searching by actor or target      More Details button in the Description column in case of long event descriptions      Faster page loading    Note  Not all search results are loaded immediately. To add more results to your search, choose Load More. Each Load More action adds up to 200 application events to your search.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-15\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 94 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Personalized Cockpit Navigation with Favorites & Recent\nDescription: We have introduced two new enhancements to navigation within SAP BTP Cockpit: Favorites & Recent, allowing you to immediately access your most important resources in the cockpit.     Favorites lets you bookmark your most important resources, saving time and effort. Nearly all pages have a favorites button on the upper right side of the page. Select the star icon to a page to your favorites.  Recent automatically adds the resources you have most recently interacted with so you can pick up where you left off.    Find all your favorites and recently visited pages by navigating to the Favorites & Recent entry in the left-side navigation panel.  For more information, check out:: Introducing Favorites and Recent in SAP BTP Cockpit - A Personalized Navigation Experience\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-17\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 95 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kubernetes,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Display of User Group and Attributes Mappings for Role Collections\nDescription: We extended the SAP BTP CLI command btp get security/role-collection by adding the --show-attribute-mappings option. When you use this option, you can display the user group and attribute mappings related to the identity providers.  For more information, see Managing Users and Their Authorizations Using the btp CLI.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: 2509a\n\n--- Record 96 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 51", " to the identity providers.  For more information, see Managing Users and Their Authorizations Using the btp CLI.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: 2509a\n\n--- Record 96 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 51.5.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 51.2.0 to 51.5.0.    https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v51.5.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v51.4.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v51.3.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-24\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: 2509a\n\n--- Record 97 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Revision 2.00.079.06\nDescription: You can now update to SAP HANA revision 2.00.079.05. See 3614625 - SAP HANA 2 SPS07 Revision 079.06.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-18\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 98 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.39.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.38.0 to 2.39.0. Updated components:       TomEE 10 is updated from version 10.1.0 to 10.1.1      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.25.10 to 2.25.12      com.fasterxml.jackson is updated from version 2.19.0 to 2.19.2      commons-lang3 is updated from version 3.17.0 to 3.18.0      commons-codec is updated from version 1.18.0 to 1.19.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-05\nValid as Of: 2025-09-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 99 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Model Manager Stability Improvements\nDescription: There have been several stability improvements related to the model manager of the Data Attribute Recommendation service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-23\nValid as Of: 2025-09-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 100 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.47.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: Improved API documentation and in-app help for Kyma dashboard (#2737).      Logs: Adjusted OTLP log agent behaviour to match legacy Fluent Bit-based setup (#2337).      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: Update to OTel Collector 0.133.0 (#2449).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 4.0.8 (#2427).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-09-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 4021 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generic Integration Flow\nDescription: The integration package Cloud Integration - Trading Partner Management V2 has been upgraded to version 2.1.0. With this update,     A new integration flow supporting the ProcessDirect adapter has been added.    A new integration flow for writing the message to the message queue has been added.    See:Integration Flow Configuration Version 2.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4022 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: ProcessDirect Adapter\nDescription: The application now supports ProcessDirect Sender and Receiver adapter.  See:     Creating a Company Profile and a Subsidiary    Creating a Trading Partner Profile  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4023 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 6.42.*  Increment: 2309  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4024 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Base Theming Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.8.0. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4025 ---\nComponent: Workflow Capability\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Renew Certificates\nDescription: Following the announcement of the root certificate replacement in SAP Business Technology Platform, we will be renewing our certificates in the upcoming weeks to be signed by DigiCert Global Root G2. This may have an impact on technical clients calling our REST APIs that do not trust DigiCert Global Root G2.  Action:   Check your trust stores  In systems where you manage the trusted certificates yourself, check if the G1 certificate exists. If it does, and its use is related to SAP BTP products, add the new G2 certificate. Don't remove the G1 certificate yet as both are needed for the transition period.  For more information, see SAP Note 3327214  and the Changing the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry environment Root Certificate Authority blog post.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4026 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Store - New Content Packages\nDescription: A new set of 21 content packages, 13 Business Content and 8 Learning Content have been added to the Store during Sep-Oct 2023. We have also made some fixes in the existing content packages.  These content packages are tailored to different lines of business such as IT, Sales, Services, Sourcing, Finance, and Procurement.  New Business Content:  SAP SuccessFactors Use Cases:    Create Permission Group      Merge User in Learning Management System (LMS)    Job Offers Approvals    Creation and Approval of Job Requisition      Creation and Approval of Mass Job Requisition      SAP S/4HANA Use Cases:    Mass Creation of Maintenance Service Orders      Ad hoc Subcontracting Purchase Requisition Creation      Journal Entry Posting Approval      Central Finance Use Cases:    Central Finance Mappings (CFIN Mapping)     Safe Deactivation Procedure for Central Finance Replication    SAP Ariba Use Case: Ariba Purchase Requisition Approval  Fixes or Patches released for Live Process Content Package: Maintain Purchase Info Record   Learning Content:  SAP S/4HANA Content:    Mass Upload of Business Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud (6PX)      In-App Configuration for SAP S4HANA Cloud Scope item J59 (6PS)      In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Items J60 and 1NT (6PT)      In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Items J45 and 18J (6PQ)        In-App Configuration for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Scope Item J58 (6PR)      Automation Anywhere:    Create a Lead in Salesforce with Automation Anywhere    Change the Opportunity Stage in Salesforce with Automation Anywhere  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-21\nValid as Of: 2023-10-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4027 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Kyma 2.19.1 - Eventing\nDescription: Event Publisher Proxy:      We’ve enhanced the readiness handling when using NATS as the eventing backend, making it more robust and reliable.      The metric previously named eventing_epp_requests_duration_milliseconds has been renamed to event", "21\nValid as Of: 2023-10-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4027 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Kyma 2.19.1 - Eventing\nDescription: Event Publisher Proxy:      We’ve enhanced the readiness handling when using NATS as the eventing backend, making it more robust and reliable.      The metric previously named eventing_epp_requests_duration_milliseconds has been renamed to eventing_epp_requests_duration_seconds to reflect its internal use of seconds as a unit. The buckets have been adjusted accordingly.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4028 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Data Extraction Process Updated\nDescription: Migration Assessment faced issues with the data extraction process. These issues have been fixed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-20\nValid as Of: 2023-10-20\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4029 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of .NET, Ruby, and R Buildpacks\nDescription: This is a reminder that the .NET, Ruby, and R offline buildpacks have been deprecated and are scheduled to be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on November 16, 2023.  If you want to continue using these buildpacks after their removal, you can use the online community buildpacks by specifying their URLs in the code of your applications. For more information, see SAP Note 3364781 .\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4030 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deletion of TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining Ciphers Postponed\nDescription: The deletion of TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining (CBC) Ciphers for the region eu20, which had received an updated timeline on October 5, 2023 and was scheduled to take place on October 19, 2023 has been postponed. It is now planned for November 16, 2023.   The following ciphers are affected:        TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256    TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA256  TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256  TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_CBC_SHA384      Note that TLS 1.3 Cipher Suites are not affected by this change.  Action:  Older clients might be affected by this change. To maintain connectivity, please check and ensure that your clients are supporting one of the following TLS 1.2 ciphers that are still supported:     TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256      TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384      TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256      TLS_DHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384      After the deletion of the deprecated ciphers, requests from older HTTP client libraries that do not include any of the supported ciphers will fail during the TLS handshake. To verify that your client can connect without CBC ciphers, you can connect it to the following test application. If the client can establish a connection to the endpoint, the server returns the message ok along with a status code 200.  Endpoint with CBC disabled: https://tls12-no-cbc.ciphers.cfapps.eu12.hana.ondemand.com\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3651 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Spatial Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: nan\nDescription:     Enhancements: Mapping API, Routing API, Geocoding API  Security updates have been implemented.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3652 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Branding and Layout\nDescription: Tenant administrator can upload an image in the administration console and use it as a logo for the applications in the tenant. See Configure Logo.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: 25497\n\n--- Record 3653 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: 25497\n\n--- Record 3654 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Upgrade Dates\nDescription: SAP Cloud Identity Services planned production releases (updates) change to every second Tuesday, 14:00 UTC from every second Wednesday, 10:00 UTC. SeeUpdates and Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-17\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: 25497\n\n--- Record 3655 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Conflict resolution error message\nDescription: The error thrown in case of failed conflict resolution is enhanced to display the attribute causing the conflict when it is provided by the target system. You can now easily identify the attribute, change its value and resolve the problem.  For more information about the conflict resolution behavior, search for properties <system prefix>user.unique.attribute in List of Properties.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3656 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Paging of provisioning systems\nDescription: Paging of source, target and proxy systems is enabled by default. As of now, the provisioning systems are sorted by type and state in an alphabetical order.  For more information, see: Search and Edit Systems\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3657 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.6.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      The first release of the Metric feature! Now, you can have a cluster-central gateway that collects metrics and pushes them via OTLP to a configured backend using the new API MetricPipeline. Additionally, three inputs are available for a pre-integrated collection of metrics. Learn more under Metrics (#13079).      A new section in the documentation features the integration guides (#575).       The setup of Fluent Bit has been simplified, resulting in an improved performance and buffer usage (#479).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-18\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3658 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Event Triggers\nDescription: You can now execute an event trigger to immediately initiate event delivery with user-provided data, using the Run now action from the Unattended triggers view. See Manage Event Triggers from the Triggers View.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-16\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3659 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Qualtrics Survey in the Enhanced Recorder\nDescription: You can now give feedback for the enhanced recorder. See: Qualtrics Survey in the Enhanced Recorder.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-16\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3660 ---\nComponent: SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Qualtrics Survey in the Enhanced Recorder\nDescription: You are now able to give feedback for the enhanced recorder. See: Qualtrics Survey in the Enhanced Recorder.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-16\nValid as Of: 2024-01-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_8749b7b67c9db3bc4a3068cd9b92d697e6470fbf2ebbc359c048e42d001a067f_v2"}